ll,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.3.stable.official [77dcf97d8]\n- Not reproducible in v4.3.stable.official [77dcf97d8]\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10 - Godot 4.4.1 stable\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen I launch Godot 4.4, the project manager displays an \"Update available\" notification for an unstable Development version of Godot (currently **4.5-dev3**).\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8194f7ec-94a5-4712-8956-68c954a3a9e3)\n\nWere one not paying attention, one could mistakenly think that whatever update is being pushed to the end-user must be stable, leading one to update Godot to an unstable version. Indeed, previous versions had the expected functionality; 4.3 encourages you to update to 4.4.1-stable.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Open Godot 4.4.1\n- Look at the bottom-right corner of the Project Manager\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n**N/A** (the bug only concerns the _Project Manager_)","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/use